# Less overengineering

Match what is already in `src/`. Do not invent a second style.

Do not add:

- Extra `type` / `interface` / `enum` / DTO classes when a small inline shape will do
- Wrapper services, helpers, or “utils” that only forward one call
- Extra modules, folders, or layers for a single new function
- Chains of calls that could be one method on the existing service
- class-validator, repositories, events, or queues until the user asks

Do:

- Put new HTTP in a thin controller; put I/O in the existing feature service (Ollama stays in `OllamaService`)
- Reuse `ConfigService` and exported module services
- One `fetch` path per integration, not parallel clients
- Inline `{ prompt?: string }` style types as in `OllamaController`

If two designs work, pick the one with fewer files and fewer types.
